// The C idiom `char[N] b = "literal";` has no working spelling in CFlat. A string literal
// is an llvm::Constant, so the bad array cast folds into a ConstantExpr the module verifier
// does not check: it compiled and then read the bytes out of the POINTER value (garbage),
// and the indexing form crashed the compiler in SelectionDAG. Rejected with its own message.
expect_error("CFlat has no C-style character-array initializer") {
    void f() { char[8] b = "hello"; b[0] = 'x'; }
}
